==English==
{{wikipedia}} [[Image:Ajedrez captura al paso del peon.png|frame|En passant in chess]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|en passant}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ɒn paˈsɒ̃/|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# in [[passing]]; [[incidentally]]; [[by the way]]

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{context|chess|lang=en}} Describing a special kind of pawn [[capture]], whereby a [[pawn]] [[capture]]s an opposing pawn immediately after it has moved forward two [[squares]] from its initial position as if it had moved only one square; the opposing pawn is captured "in [[passing]] through" the usual square from where it would ordinarily be liable to be captured.

